# Every (fusion, quantity) that owes no sum. One row per pair: composition/suspended_fusions.sqlc
# with each ground that lifts every quantity spread over the quantities it lifts.
#
# A NULL quantity is every quantity
#   A suspension ground names the one quantity it lifts, or none, meaning all of them: nobody
#   searched the fusion for double counting, a conversion was never sized, a part resolves to
#   nothing here. Every reader asking whether one quantity of a fusion is suspended would have to
#   spell that out as `quantity IS NULL OR quantity = <that one>`; spread once over
#   `pm.summed_quantity`, the answer is a row or no row.
#
# Each pair once
#   A fusion can be suspended on a ground naming no quantity and on one naming demand, and the
#   spreading then reaches (fusion, demand) twice. The pair is suspended once, so the relation has
#   no repeats on its key; composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc keeps every ground and its reason.
#
# Checked by
#   algebra/suspended_quantities.sqlc holds it against the spreading written the long way.
-- composition/suspended_fusions.sqlc spread over pm.summed_quantity.
SELECT DISTINCT s.composition, s.composed_layer, q.quantity
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/suspended_fusions.sqlc)
) s
JOIN      unnest(enum_range(NULL::pm.summed_quantity)) AS q(quantity)
       ON s.quantity IS NULL OR s.quantity = q.quantity
